a) perform comprehensive review of Group's current coverage;
b) perform preliminary overview on our risk profile;
c) make initial suggestions for optimal coverage. 

Nevertheless we need a professional risk consultant/underwriter with experience in corporate risk underwriting to provide a comprehensive overview of our risk profile and suggest the best solutions/coverage keeping in mind the specifics of our business. So I would word additional points for myself to supplement the above:
d) prep-work for finding the candidates for such consultant; 
e) co-ordination with the consultant; 
f) support to management for choosing optimal coverage and finding suitable insurance partners/solutions (if applicable);

Nevertheless I see as the first part of the task point a, i.e mapping.
What I can see from the GDrive is that contract-documents/policies are owned by many different persons without considerable logic regarding the ownership. So first of all, should I turn to management to get a comprehensive input across the Group, or do you suggest any other way to start?

I suggest we agree on the precise action-plan and timetable by the end of October after I am back from vacation, and you have had time to review the above and provide feedback.

