{color:#500050}{color}{color:black}1) {color}{color:#500050} {color}{color:#333333} *Art. 6 *{color}{color:#500050} {color}{color:#333333}is very general and does not establish how to complete the payment in the case of voluntary termination. Our legal team suggests to:{color}{color:#500050}{color}

{color:#500050}{color}{color:#333333}a) add a price to each deliverable in the annex and then we then add a statement to  *Art.6*  that  _in the event that either party elects to terminate early, the only amount owed with be to cover the cost of deliverables which the Client considers to have been fully completed,_  or{color}{color:#500050}{color}{color:#333333}{color}{color:#500050}{color}

{color:#500050}{color}{color:#333333}b) add the statement to  *Art.6*  that  _in the event that either party elects to terminate early, the only amount owed will be determined at the discretion of the Client_.{color}{color:#500050}{color}

{color:#500050}{color}{color:#333333}2) We propose to add the following to  *Art.6*:{color}{color:#500050}{color}

{color:#500050} {color}{color:#333333} _Either contracting Party may at any time terminate this Contract with immediate effect and with no liability to make any further payment if there has been a material breach of any of the obligations._{color}{color:#500050}{color}{color:#333333}{color} {color:#500050}{color}

{color:#500050} {color}{color:#333333} _Any of the Client's property in possession of the Agency and any original, digital, or copy documents obtained by the Agency in the course of providing the services shall be returned, to the opposite Party, or if digital deleted, at any time on request and in any event on or before the termination of this agreement._{color}{color:#500050}{color} 

{color:#500050} {color}

{color:#500050}{color}{color:#333333}3) The last paragraph of  *Art. 8*  states:{color}{color:#500050}{color}

{color:#500050} {color}{color:#333333} _In case of a breach of the provisions of article 6, the breaching party undertakes to compensate the other party for an amount equal to the gross salary or to the gross fees which the partner or the labor would receive during these two years. The compensation which is defined by the present Contract between the contracting parties is considered to be reasonable and fair and responds to their actual damage._{color}{color:#500050}{color} 

{color:#500050} {color}

{color:#500050}{color}{color:#333333}This is not valid for the current contract (e.g. “two years”). We propose to remove the last paragraph and handle the termination in Article 6 as proposed above.{color}{color:#500050}{color}{color:#500050}{color}

