Hey Evelin, in signatory policy it is stated that signatory authority can be deligated for employment contracts in the following way:

5.1.2.

a) 	Country Manager - for employees employed in respective country;
b)	Expansion Manager - for employees employed by Group Entities of their region;
c) 	HQ Head of Division - for employees employed into their reporting line regardless of employing Group Entity;
d) 	Head of People & Culture - for all employees regardless of their reporting line or employing Group Entity;
e) 	Legal Counsel in HQ - for all employees regardless of their reporting line or employing Group Entity.

Hey Evelin! I think we have reviewed this question now a few times with various members of the P&C team but for final clarification rule of thumb is as follows:

* Our internal signatory policy states that employment contract signatory deligation can be made in the following manner--> 
5.1.2. 	Employment contracts as well as any agreement to amend or terminate the employment contract:

a) 	Country Manager - for employees employed in respective country;
b)	Expansion Manager - for employees employed by Group Entities of their region;
c) 	HQ Head of Division - for employees employed into their reporting line regardless of employing Group Entity;
d) 	Head of People & Culture - for all employees regardless of their reporting line or employing Group Entity;
e) 	Legal Counsel in HQ - for all employees regardless of their reporting line or employing Group Entity.

* It should be confirmed with the local firm that this internal policy authorization is enough to do so. If it is not then a PoA should be drafted deligating someone from HQ the power to do so. The firm should be able to provide this guidance. 

